#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, liveness, loop]
# doc: |
#   RV-F #14 (for-var vs body-local, ACCEPT direction). `s` is a FRESH local
#   declared INSIDE the loop body, so it is re-created each iteration and IS
#   loop-local — moving it out with `consume(!s)` is legal on every iteration.
#   This is the deliberate contrast to reject_for_var_move_in_loop.gg, where the
#   `for`-element variable aliases persistent collection storage and is NOT
#   loop-local (moving it is E_MoveInLoop). The two fixtures pin the distinction
#   the oracle now keys on the TYPED bind source (`Source::BorrowView` = the
#   for-desugar's element view → not loop-local; a user `Source::Copy` body-local
#   → loop-local) rather than any shape heuristic.
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "done\n"
#!end

void consume(String !s):
    pass

void main():
    Vector[int] items = [1, 2]
    for i in items:
        String s = "fresh"
        consume(!s)
    print("done")
